---
description: >-
  The markdownAlwaysOn twin of label-syntax.mmd: the same swimlane labels
  with the setting on, so every label is markdown. The plain **bold**
  _ital_ lane titles, node texts and edge labels draw bold and italic, the
  bare backticks and the code span draw inline code; tags, \n and quoted
  markdown strings draw as in the default picture, which this one differs
  from.
config:
  markdownAlwaysOn: true
---
swimlane-beta LR
  subgraph L1[lane **bold** _ital_]
    A[node **bold** _ital_]
  end
  subgraph L2["`lane **bold** _ital_`"]
    B["`node **bold** _ital_`"]
  end
  subgraph L3[`lane **bold** _ital_`]
    C[`node **bold** _ital_`]
  end
  subgraph L4[lane a `code` b]
    D[node a `code` b]
  end
  subgraph L5[lane <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O]
    E[node <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O]
  end
  subgraph L6[lane one\ntwo]
    F[node one\ntwo]
  end
  A -->|edge **bold** _ital_| B
  B -->|"`edge **bold** _ital_`"| C
  C -->|`edge **bold** _ital_`| D
  D -->|edge a `code` b| E
  E -->|edge <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O| F
  F -->|edge one\ntwo| A
